  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Saving Medicines : Improving Access and Quality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve medicines regulation by providing support to regionally developed and approved plans to (i) strengthen the capacity of national medicines regulatory agencies to carry out their core functions, such as the effective registration of new products and monitoring of quality and (ii) work more collaboratively together to increase efficiencies and reduce transaction costs (for countries and pharmaceutical companies alike) in the regulation of medicines by 31 March 2015. This contributes to our MDG 8 target 17 to provide access to affordable essential drugs in developing countries</narrative>
  </description>
